WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:06.110
Batman is often treated like a god among mortal
superheroes by dedicated comic fans.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:11.040
After all, he's basically a genius ninja detective
billionaire with enough money to build weapons

00:00:11.040 --> 00:00:15.450
designed to beat the most powerful heroes
and villains in the DC Universe.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:20.220
Still, comics writers like to remind readers
that Batman is totally capable of having his

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:23.179
bat-butt kicked up and down the streets of
Gotham.

00:00:23.179 --> 00:00:26.909
Even though he always bounces back, let's
take a look at some of the heroes and villains

00:00:26.909 --> 00:00:29.579
that have destroyed Batman.

00:00:29.579 --> 00:00:31.220
Bane

00:00:31.220 --> 00:00:35.611
Let's start with the obvious one: the big
bad guy that beat Batman so badly that it

00:00:35.611 --> 00:00:37.280
made the evening news.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:43.230
In the summer of 1993, DC kicked off a major
Batman event called Knightfall, in which Batman

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:47.920
becomes burnt out after Bane releases all
of his greatest villains from Arkham Asylum

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:48.920
at once.

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:53.210
While Bats is overworked and overstressed,
Bane discovers that the Dark Knight is Bruce

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:56.920
Wayne — which leads to a violent showdown
in the Batcave.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:01:01.739
Things don't go well for Batman: Bane dominates
the fight against a weakened Caped Crusader.

00:01:01.739 --> 00:01:06.120
He lifts Batman over his head and brings him
crashing down over his knee, breaking Batman's

00:01:06.120 --> 00:01:08.690
back and putting him completely out of commission.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:12.660
It's become such an iconic takedown, that
it made its way to the big screen in The Dark

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:13.420
Knight Rises:

00:01:17.090 --> 00:01:21.180
It really is the most devastating hit that
Batman has ever taken — but it's not the

00:01:21.191 --> 00:01:23.150
only one.

00:01:23.150 --> 00:01:24.650
Superman

00:01:24.650 --> 00:01:29.110
Even within the ridiculous medium of comics,
where anything is possible, it takes a lot

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:34.110
to believe Batman has a realistic shot at
defeating Superman in a one-on-one fight,

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:37.690
but somehow, Batman often seems to come out
on top.

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:39.360
Often...but not always.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:43.570
There was the time villain Maxwell Lord made
Superman hallucinate that he was battling

00:01:43.570 --> 00:01:48.570
Darkseid in a gladiatorial arena, when in
reality he was beating on Batman so badly

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:50.430
that Bruce ended up in a coma.

00:01:50.430 --> 00:01:55.210
In the story Lex Luthor: Man of Steel, Batman
is planning to attack Superman with kryptonite…

00:01:55.210 --> 00:02:00.060
only to have Supes literally blow the rock
out of Batman's hand, then pound Batman to

00:02:00.060 --> 00:02:01.600
within an inch of his life, again.

00:02:01.600 --> 00:02:06.520
Or how about the time an alien parasite called
Blackrock took over Batman's body, granting

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.170
him superhuman strength, flight, and a whole
lot of crazy?

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:14.500
Even fighting a Batman with super powers,
Superman was able to punch the parasite right

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.600
out of his body.

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:16.600
By the way!

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.910
Punching is typically not a good solution
for dealing with parasites.

00:02:20.910 --> 00:02:22.260
Wonder Woman

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:27.590
In the 2016 graphic novel Wonder Woman: The
Hiketeia, Batman is on the hunt for a woman

00:02:27.590 --> 00:02:31.330
responsible for the deaths of sex slavers
and drug dealers in Gotham.

00:02:31.330 --> 00:02:35.520
And she just so happens to be the very same
person Wonder Woman has been honor-bound to

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:36.520
protect.

00:02:36.520 --> 00:02:41.060
When the two titans of the DC universe collide,
things get ugly — mostly for Batman.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:44.740
Diana beats him into submission and stands
with a foot on his head.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:49.070
If that isn't the ultimate symbol of Batman
getting owned, we don't know what is.

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:53.710
He escapes by invoking an Amazonian ritual,
but it's a pretty close call.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:54.750
Prometheus

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:58.120
Though he's a villain you don't hear much
about…

00:02:58.120 --> 00:03:00.580
"Oh no, Promootheus!"

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:01.840
"Prometheus!"

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:06.330
...Prometheus is Batman's twisted mirror image,
and in an even more literal way than Joker

00:03:06.330 --> 00:03:07.330
or Two-Face.

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:11.780
Batman's family was gunned down by a street
thug, but Prometheus' parents were criminals

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:15.480
killed by the police, leading him to swear
vengeance upon those who attempt to bring

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:16.900
justice to the world.

00:03:16.900 --> 00:03:21.420
Like Batman, he's a trained fighter, he's
filthy rich, and he's got a sharp mind.

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:25.470
But despite sharing the same name, he has
very little to do with the Prometheus who

00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:27.310
makes an appearance in the Arrowverse.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:32.290
Prometheus masquerades as the hero Retro and
walks straight into the Justice League's Watchtower

00:03:32.290 --> 00:03:36.660
with a helmet that grants him the skills of
the 30 greatest martial artists in the world,

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:37.740
including Batman.

00:03:37.740 --> 00:03:41.910
He then beats the snot out of everyone, and
his trouncing of the Justice League only ends

00:03:41.910 --> 00:03:44.870
when Catwoman whips him in the nethers.

00:03:44.870 --> 00:03:46.200
Deacon Blackfire

00:03:46.200 --> 00:03:50.540
The Cult is one of the darkest, most brutal
stories in the Batman canon, thanks to the

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:55.200
vicious Deacon Blackfire, leader of a cult
of Gotham's homeless, who've been brainwashed

00:03:55.200 --> 00:03:56.960
into doing his murderous bidding.

00:03:56.960 --> 00:04:01.410
During his investigation into the cult, Batman
is captured by Deacon's forces and spends

00:04:01.410 --> 00:04:06.030
a huge chunk of the tale being tortured…
and kissed gently on the cheek… while high

00:04:06.030 --> 00:04:07.340
on psychotropic drugs.

00:04:07.340 --> 00:04:12.350
It's all an attempt to brainwash Batman into
fighting for Blackfire's underground army.

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:16.609
Batman's eventually saved by Robin, but not
before being reduced to a sobbing husk of

00:04:16.609 --> 00:04:19.809
his former self, and having his entire worldview
shattered.

00:04:19.809 --> 00:04:20.809
The best part?

00:04:20.809 --> 00:04:25.749
Robin finally gets Batman back for all of
those meme-friendly slaps to the face.

00:04:25.749 --> 00:04:30.529
Blackfire isn't even the only opponent to
use drugs to take down Batman, either.

00:04:30.529 --> 00:04:31.659
Swamp Thing

00:04:31.659 --> 00:04:36.039
You might think that Swamp Thing is a joke,
and if you've ever heard his old cartoon theme

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:37.280
song, you wouldn't be wrong.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:43.960
"Swamp Thing… you are ama-zing."

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:48.920
Bad cartoons aside, Swamp Thing isn't just
one of the most fascinating characters in

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:52.210
all of DC comics — he's also one of the
most powerful.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:55.939
In fact, he's won pretty much every fight
he and Batman have gotten into.

00:04:55.939 --> 00:05:00.990
When Batman chases Killer Croc into Swamp
Thing's… uh, swamp, the big green guy takes

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:03.879
out Bats with a puff of hallucinogenic pollen.

00:05:03.879 --> 00:05:08.650
The most memorable beatdown happened in Swamp
Thing #53, when the muck man's wife is in

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:12.500
police custody and he responds by turning
Gotham into a jungle.

00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:16.849
When Batman confronts him, Swampy divides
himself into many Swamp Things and just beats

00:05:16.849 --> 00:05:19.979
the snot out of Batman like it's a gang initiation
ritual.

00:05:19.979 --> 00:05:23.330
Poor Batman never had a bat-chance.

00:05:23.330 --> 00:05:24.749
Deathstroke

00:05:24.749 --> 00:05:29.240
Slade Wilson is one of the deadliest characters
in any comic book universe, regardless of

00:05:29.240 --> 00:05:30.240
the publisher.

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:34.309
He was the world's greatest killer even before
the government experimented on him, making

00:05:34.309 --> 00:05:35.470
him even deadlier.

00:05:35.470 --> 00:05:39.021
One of his first fights after getting his
own comic book in the early '90s was with

00:05:39.021 --> 00:05:40.021
Batman.

00:05:40.021 --> 00:05:43.620
At this point the Dark Knight was already
something of a legend, able to defeat any

00:05:43.620 --> 00:05:45.210
foe that crossed his path.

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:50.120
So, it was kind of a big deal when Deathstroke
and Batman threw down in an old-school fistfight,

00:05:50.120 --> 00:05:54.039
and Deathstroke beat him into unconsciousness
by tossing him into a bookshelf.

00:05:54.039 --> 00:05:58.409
The only reason Batman is alive today is because
Deathstroke spared him, and they ended up

00:05:58.409 --> 00:06:01.960
hanging around together for a couple of issues
afterwards.

00:06:01.960 --> 00:06:03.570
Lady Shiva

00:06:03.570 --> 00:06:07.680
The assassin known as Lady Shiva is one of
the greatest martial artists in the world,

00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:09.509
according to Batman himself.

00:06:09.509 --> 00:06:14.650
When she's not an ally of Batman, she's kicking
his butt, like in the pages of Nightwing #0,

00:06:14.650 --> 00:06:18.530
when Shiva did battle with both Batman and
Dick Grayson at the same time.

00:06:18.530 --> 00:06:23.249
She downed Batman with a poison-tipped shuriken,
then beat up Dick until she felt sorry for

00:06:23.249 --> 00:06:24.839
him, and offered to train him.

00:06:24.839 --> 00:06:29.129
He declined, but it was Lady Shiva's influence
that convinced Dick Grayson to stop being

00:06:29.129 --> 00:06:31.110
Robin and become his own man.

00:06:31.110 --> 00:06:33.710
It was then that he decided to become Nightwing.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:38.539
Not too many career decisions come from watching
someone beat up your dad, but hey — comic

00:06:38.539 --> 00:06:40.460
books are weird.

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:41.460
Joker

00:06:41.460 --> 00:06:45.979
Crushing Batman psychologically and pushing
him to the edge of his own sanity is the Joker's

00:06:45.979 --> 00:06:50.139
primary objective, and the list of Joker's
offenses is disturbing and endless.

00:06:50.139 --> 00:06:54.289
But the only time that the Joker has been
able to completely destroy Batman was when

00:06:54.289 --> 00:06:57.430
he stole the awesome power of an interdimensional
imp.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:07:02.569
Using the abilities of Superman antagonist
Mr. Mxyzptlk, Joker warps reality to kill

00:07:02.569 --> 00:07:08.309
Batman over and over… until Superman makes
him realize that even though Joker is all-powerful,

00:07:08.309 --> 00:07:10.680
he just can't bear to let go of Batman.

00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:15.270
"No, you... you complete me."

00:07:15.270 --> 00:07:17.160
Darkseid

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:21.979
It's not surprising that someone like Darkseid,
who's basically a god, can take out a flesh

00:07:21.979 --> 00:07:23.530
and blood mortal like Batman.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:27.059
What was surprising, however, was just how
Darkseid did it.

00:07:27.059 --> 00:07:32.249
During the Final Crisis storyline, it looked
like Darkseid simply fried Batman to a crisp

00:07:32.249 --> 00:07:33.520
with his weird eye lasers.

00:07:33.520 --> 00:07:37.509
Of course, no one really ever stays dead in
comic books for long...

00:07:37.509 --> 00:07:42.229
As it happened, Darkseid replaced Batman's
body with a dead clone — fooling Superman

00:07:42.229 --> 00:07:47.300
and most of his Superfriends — and sent
the real Batman traveling uncontrollably through

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:48.300
time.

00:07:48.300 --> 00:07:49.330
Why would he bother with all of that?

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:53.699
Because Batman was turned into a weapon, whose
forced time-travel adventures threatened to

00:07:53.699 --> 00:07:55.800
undo all of reality.

00:07:55.800 --> 00:07:59.780
Eventually Batman — with a lot of help from
the Justice League — managed to escape back

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:02.490
to the present day without destroying all
of existence.

00:08:02.490 --> 00:08:06.800
Still, the important thing to keep in mind
is that he got his butt kicked — and all

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:08.840
it took was a single glance.

00:08:08.840 --> 00:08:11.270
"Holy spontaneous combustion!"

00:08:11.270 --> 00:08:12.270
Thanks for watching!

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:15.129
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:08:15.129 --> 00:08:17.740
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

